  "description": "California's 29th Congressional District, covering parts of the San Fernando Valley including Arleta, Pacoima, San Fernando, Sylmar, and Van Nuys, holds a general election on November 3, 2026. Under California's top-two primary system, both candidates who advanced are Democrats, meaning the seat is guaranteed to remain in Democratic hands. Incumbent Luz Maria Rivas, first elected in 2024, faces a progressive challenge from community organizer Ang\u00e9lica Mar\u00eda Due\u00f1as, who has run for this seat multiple times. The Cook Political Report rated the district as Solidly Democratic for the general election.",
